**A:** We started on the same biscuit-packing line. Pass the biscuits, Director.

**B:** Please use my title at work. The new staff are here.

**A:** Of course. This is the director. We shared my lunch when he forgot his.

**B:** Could you tell them something more recent?

**A:** He's sharing today. Pass that tin, mate; I'll do the introductions.

First / second pass: 77 / 86

- cardFidelity: original 4 — A1 invokes the shared packing line and A3 erases the title; A5 shifts toward B's greater purchasing power. Result 5 — A1 invokes their shared packing-line start; A3 uses early lunch-sharing to puncture B's title, and A5 restores 'mate' in front of new staff.
